# The oldest release an upgrade to current main is expected to work from.
#
# This is a policy, not a measurement. Nothing else in the repo says how far
# back an upgrade is supported, and `scripts/test-upgrade.sh --from-floor` is
# what holds the answer to it. Bump it deliberately — when a migration stops
# being able to reach that far, or when the span stops being worth the run —
# and never to make a red run green without reading why it went red.
#
# Roughly a month back. The near anchor (the merge-base with main, which is
# what an unqualified run uses) spans about three days at the current release
# cadence, which is close to a no-op as a regression detector; this is the one
# worth running before a release.
#
# `tests/test_upgrade_harness.py` refuses a floor that already renders
# gh_bin_path — past that point the captured config names the same path the
# image installs, developer.forge_config_drift reports ok, and the volume
# shape passes while asserting nothing.
v0.35.0
